# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files to CRLF on
# checkout. That is fine for Python and JavaScript, and fatal for anything a Linux container
# executes: a shell script whose shebang line ends in CR is read as "#!/bin/sh\r", and the kernel
# reports "no such file or directory" for an interpreter that plainly exists - one of the more
# confusing failures to debug from a Docker build log.
#
# So the files that end up inside a container are pinned to LF regardless of platform.

# Let Git decide for everything not named below.
* text=auto

# Executed inside the Linux images - MUST stay LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerignore text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf

# nginx refuses to parse a config with stray CRs in some directives.
*.conf text eol=lf

# Read by cron on the host, same shebang/parsing concern as above.
deploy/crontab.example text eol=lf

# PowerShell is fine with either, but CRLF is the platform norm for it.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary - never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xls binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
